s10-5-p22 = prose (cons "A JIT may specialize a continuing process further when new static facts become available. A new artifact \(a_1\) may be installed beside an old artifact \(a_0\), but replacing an *active* occurrence is a migration of its current continuation, not a restart of its original source program. For a source continuation \(k\), let \(\mathsf{Boundary}_i(k)\) contain target states of artifact \(a_i\) at which the correspondence with \(k\) is known (for example a proved turn boundary or a suspended command-response boundary). Let \(\mathsf{LiveRel}_i(d,k,H,T,S)\) state that target state \(d\) realizes \(k\) with already-issued effect history \(H\), outstanding token set \(T\), and retained snapshot \(S\). Given a dependency certificate \(D_1\), the swap evidence is a map" nil)
